Image prompt rules: describe only what IS visible; never use negating words because the image model ignores them and draws the thing anyway; describe what is there instead of what is missing. Whatever the subject, name at least two details particular to this world and its peoples, drawn from their account, so the image shows this world rather than a generic stock scene, in the look the world itself calls for, whether grounded or fantastic. Describe the content, light and composition only; never name an artistic medium, art style, camera or lens, because the world's chosen image style is applied to every prompt separately.
